{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/19408-what-arcanoi-and-arts-are-we-missing","id":19408,"title":"What Arcanoi and Arts are we missing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-27T16:01:42-08:00","id":19408,"title":"What Arcanoi and Arts are we missing?","content":"The Arts of Changeling were fun, I liked how Blood Dimmed Tied and other supplements would add to them. What powers do you feel we are missing? I feel we need something for a more sorcery vibe, or maybe some sort of High Ritual magic? We definitely need mechanics for crafting Treasures.<br /> <br /> The Arcanoi in Wraith were cool too since there was a huge Population of Wraiths compared to all the other Supernatural beings, it feels like we need a greater variety of Arcanoi. And they really need to fix Phantasmagoria, seriously its confusing and doesn't work. It doesn't really even have a mechanic, even Chimeristry is more complex. You can take a human soul while they dream? The hell? How do you drop that power without explaining the mechanics further. We needed some method for making stronger Wraiths, because they made it seem like Powerful Wraiths was solely in the purview of NPCs, like Deathlords with high Traits, and the Ferrymen with their unique ritual magic. But there are a lot of Arcanos I would like to see. I think the first homebrew I made was a Vengeance Arcanos themed after Ghost Rider, that was like 8 years ago I definitely would like to return to clean that up after W20 comes out. One thing that fills a lot of holes for me is allowing Wraiths to use Sorcery, that finally makes their vast supply of Knowledge from Lost Libraries definitely useful. We could use a powertrait or some method of having traits past 5, and high level Arcanoi.<br /> <br /> So what Arts and Arcanoi would you like to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:34:32-08:00","id":28143,"title":"","content":"I think Elemental Arcanoi would be pretty cool, Revlid did a set of Underworld Elements that reminded me of Geist, and I think it would be cool if wraiths had some Elementals powers like this. I know they have some fire stuff, but just a lil. But due to their primordial nature you could even make them not part of the Western Guild structure, you could use some more ancient ideas like mystery cults, kind of like how Pandemonium was developed by some greek Pandora Cults.<br /> <br /> Maybe an Art for Controlling Shadows and or the Dead, either as a single art or multiple arts. It works hella well for the Lost. Maybe a Stars Art, that could have some pretty cool mythic resonance and would be one of the more &quot;magical&quot; of the magic Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:47:24-08:00","id":28780,"title":"","content":"While some of those things sound... potentially cool, I sorta like the idea that wraiths are too entropic to really develop that sort of thing on their own. Do they have access to old libraries? Sure. Do they have the ability to turn that knowledge into powerz? <i>Maybe</i>. Because they've been around so long, probably, but I imagine some things are just too much for wraiths. I mean, look at the way they treat (for example) users of Catharsis - and that's a <i>helpful</i> power. Now imagine the way they would treat someone who tried to manipulate spectres.<br /> <br /> That said, they do have some interaction with other splats, so maybe some way of taking advantage of that. A &quot;you're not going to rape my soul, stupid Giovanni&quot; Arcanos (after all, half a millennium of being treated as a vampire's bitch is probably enough to come up with a way to fight 'em) or an arcanos that allows them to travel the Black Paths of Balor (somehow). Even, yes, a way to control the dead (although that's pushing it - I mean, there are already Risen).<br /> <br /> As for elemental powers and magic, not sure that fits the spirit of the game <i>or</i> makes sense for cWoD wraiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T09:06:57-07:00","id":90932,"title":"","content":"Well Wraith does have a bunch of Storm based elemental powers due to Maelstrom's prominence in the setting, as well as some fire powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would really like some alternate powers for the Exotic Arcanoi. The Way of the Soul and the Way of the Scholar have some awesome potential. And Tempered Arcanoi (basically combo powers) would fill some really awesome gaps! Like Moliating/Soulforging/Jadecrafting a wraith combining Pandemonium into the effect could make for things like blood fountains, or burning trees. I could see making some of the unique properties of places like Tiyu, or the Labyrinth when combining Pandemonium and Argos, maybe into the very foundation of the structure to create that distorting time and space effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> The books say there is a bunch of alternate Powers, literally hundreds of them, in existence and the only ones given are just a sample. So I think a lot of innovations are possible that are just waiting to be made. Such as combining Way of the Merchant/Farmer to do things like create permanent Pathos Money using the cultivated corpus farmed from Kuei.<br /> <br /> The Chains of the Emperor seem like they would ripe for a bunch of badass powers, like making its user double in size, or have perfect coordination with a unit of guardsmen.<br /> <br /> And I would imagine Way of the Soul would also be found in Swar with their connection to the various enlightenment seeking religions.<br /> <br /> A collection of cool exotic Artifacts would be cool as they could perform things normally unknown to the Arcanoi, such as creating rain, or taming the Tempest into an Isle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T17:36:46-07:00","id":91237,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the power from Orpheus where you reach into the Maelstrom and pull something out. Kinda like Argos, but in reverse. &quot;I reach in and pull out a hammer.&quot; &quot;You get the sole of a old boot. But the heel looks like it's sturdy enough to pound a nail. Maybe....&quot;<br /> &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T18:56:21-07:00","id":91312,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/19408-what-arcanoi-and-arts-are-we-missing?p=91237#post91237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the power from Orpheus where you reach into the Maelstrom and pull something out. Kinda like Argos, but in reverse. &quot;I reach in and pull out a hammer.&quot; &quot;You get the sole of a old boot. But the heel looks like it's sturdy enough to pound a nail. Maybe....&quot;<br /> &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That power is in <i>Dark Reflection: Spectres</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T10:38:19-07:00","id":91723,"title":"","content":"It showed up both places: Tempest-Weaving in Specters and parts of Storm-Wending in Orpheus. In Specter it was a stepping stone to being the set masters for Harrowings. In Orpheus it was a part of a Argos, Flux and other ideas mash-up. <br /> <br /> I think there's room for a whole Arcanoi here. Sorta the opposite of Argos - instead of jumping into the Tempest, you reach in and pull something out. The spectral version of it would be Tempest-Weaving but would still head in the same direction. The wraithly version would be some kind of &quot;finding lost things&quot;. <br /> <br /> Just an idea that has been floating around since I ran Wraith and was looking through Orpheus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:49:26-07:00","id":93641,"title":"","content":"I think what you are looking for would be a valid variant power of Argos actually. We never really got any. As far as Arcanoi goes, there are already plenty. There are 13 basic Arcanoi, 3 &quot;lost&quot;/&quot;hidden&quot; Acanoi, 2 Risen specific Arcanoi that could honestly work for any Wraith, 8 Dark Arcanoi, and a smattering of weird foreign ghost abilities that honestly don't seem to make sense and are somewhat redundant. That is a lot. Several could stand to be reworked. Phantasm needs to be a bit better explained. Embody needs to be made more useful for what it does. Other powers need toning down. I think we still have a pretty big buffet of powers to choose from though, and almost all of them classically ghosty. I would really hate to pile-on a bunch of unthematic crap just to add more powers for the sake of adding more powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T12:10:30-07:00","id":93667,"title":"","content":"I count something like 18 Arts. Several are good, although I feel many authors of later Arts seemed to forget that Arts should have various effects depending on what Realm they are combined with, as opposed to one off effects that depend on a single Realm combination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:09:17-07:00","id":94489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/19408-what-arcanoi-and-arts-are-we-missing?p=93667#post93667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I count something like 18 Arts. Several are good, although I feel many authors of later Arts seemed to forget that Arts should have various effects depending on what Realm they are combined with, as opposed to one off effects that depend on a single Realm combination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's true it seemed they forgot that the cool creativity of Arts were supposed to be reflected in their pairing with Realms. But I really like how they tried to fill in missing Niches, like the arts in the Blood Dimmed tides were coolsville. You could have put the cold art and the weather art in the same art, but nope they got their own separate arts, which I like because it opened up what you could do with each theme. I would like a revision of the Spirit Link art though as it was tied to ancestors as well as the spirit world. It would be for instance if we got a Necromancy Art, as that is a gap in classical wizardry for dem fairies. Either a single Necromancy art for the Dead, the Underworld, Ghosts, and Darkness, or split it into an art for Ghosts and the Underworld, an Art for deadthings and bones, and an art for shadows and Darkness. We could also use some sort of Plant Mastery Art. And I surely wouldn't complain if we got more Kith Arts, like maybe one for Trolls pertaining to things like Mountains/Stones/Strength/Honor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:42:11-07:00","id":94573,"title":"","content":"How about an Arcanos that deals with helping resolve fetters, etc.? Some way to help lift drones up? Even redeem specters (at high levels)? <br /> <br /> Something that the Heretics had before they were Heretics. Back in the days of the Fishers, etc. And something the Hierarchy would NOT approve of. If drones can be made conscious again, it might make it harder to melt them down, etc. It could undermine the whole economy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:51:55-07:00","id":94578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/19408-what-arcanoi-and-arts-are-we-missing?p=94573#post94573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about an Arcanos that deals with helping resolve fetters, etc.? Some way to help lift drones up? Even redeem specters (at high levels)?<br /> <br /> Something that the Heretics had before they were Heretics. Back in the days of the Fishers, etc. And something the Hierarchy would NOT approve of. If drones can be made conscious again, it might make it harder to melt them down, etc. It could undermine the whole economy...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's a very cool idea, that would be an interesting secret back in the days of the Fisher.<br /> <br /> We could also I guess split them up as alternate and alloyed powers between the existing Arcanoi. Lifeweb already has to deal with Fetters and Passions so such a power to help resolve a fetter could go there. Uplifting a Drone would be an awesome idea for maybe a alloyed power. And I was always for redeeming specters, so a high level Castigate/alloyed power. So yeah I think it would be cool as a new Arcanos as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T00:47:05-07:00","id":94768,"title":"","content":"Resolving Fetters can be alt arts for Lifeweb, and redeeming spectres can, and I believe is, an alt art for Castigate. Uplifting a drone...I kind of like that being an alt Usury power, as uplifting in Orpheus was just a matter of pumping Pathos/Corpus (Vitality) into a drone. [br][/br] There isn't really an Arcanos that deals with Passions directly. Lifeweb does not, to my knowledge, affect Passions. Keening, Intimate, and Mnemosynis sort of deal with it indirectly, but that's it. of course that might be to prevent the wholesale rewriting of character motivation. It's also hard to have dissenters to your government if you can just magically make them not want to be dissenters anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T00:52:10-07:00","id":94773,"title":"","content":"Yes, the level five Castigate power <b>Shadow Wrack</b> from the Pardoners/Puppeteers Guildbook can be used to redeem Spectres, or at least move them closer to redemption. Also someday I'll get to make paragraph breaks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T01:01:20-07:00","id":94777,"title":"","content":"I guess I really need to get Orpheus eventually. I would really like some more information on the evolution process of becoming a Malfean, we just get a very brief explanation that Specters often cannibalize souls, eventually bloat into a mindless Hekatonhire, and eventually evolve intelligence and further power. It would be need to have a systems/power to represent this, so we can say portray specters at the various rungs of the Ascent to Malfeanhood.<br /> <br /> I'm really not a fan of NPCs like Charon, and Yu-Huang can only pull of these tricks cause they are special. That's why it kind of feels like we Need at least a level 6 for Arcanoi to represent folks like the Lady of Fate, Charon, or Malfeans. Though I guess Alloyed Arcanoi can make up for some of this, but they can only combine two powers thus limiting how mind boggling you get with them. It just seems kinda lame to say one Master of Fatalism or Inhabit is better then all other masters of the same level.<br /> <br /> And it seems odd that we get hints of the Deathlords stats, like the weakened Smiling Lords stats and its waaaay higher then say Coldheart's stats, for some reason Coldheart wasn't big on going past the human limit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T22:27:27-07:00","id":98960,"title":"","content":"You can take a look at Coldheart's human backstory for a hint at why he wasn't big on exceeding normal human limits :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}